  "2026-10-24T07:07:17.502Z","harness:codex","Intake validation: build passed. Tracker context quality has zero blocking findings with the existing graph-degree advisory; graph composition and append-only record integrity pass. The latest installed external pm-changelog generator check passes with no changelog change because this issue is open. Reporter source, expected and observed results, runtime versions, acceptance criteria, estimate, and semantic lineage are recorded. No production fix or independent reproduction is claimed. The item remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-24T07:23:02.161Z","harness:codex","PR1572 CodeRabbit review correction: checked the original reporter source and distinguished the SDK get message (Unknown get --fields value(s): probe_score) from the CLI get/list/search structured unknown_field_projection refusal. The source body remains intact. This is an intake accuracy fix only; the issue stays open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-24T09:41:58.932Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: reuse canonical SDK and package-platform lineage; inspect active extension item_fields separately from runtime schema fields, then extend shared projection validation without importing query runtimes into contract-only modules. Preserve value types, unknown-field refusal, and activation isolation. Full all-status strict corpus read: 3094 items, 2806 closed, no omissions or unreadables. Current GitHub has no open PRs or dependency/security alerts; every open issue already has a PM-link comment."
  "2026-10-24T09:48:23.250Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: the new isolated SDK/CLI fixture failed before the fix with unknown_field_projection for all six declared custom types, after a full get proved they were stored. After using the existing canonical collectRegisteredItemFieldNames helper in all three SDK validators, typed zero/false/empty/container values and prefixed selectors pass SDK, CLI and native action dispatch. Unknown-field recovery retains valid custom selectors and disabled-extension reads refuse without registration leakage."
  "2026-10-24T09:54:58.084Z","harness:codex","Latest package acceptance: installed pm-changelog2026.10.24 from the public npm registry, matching the latest exact published version. Package doctor has zero activation failures or blocking findings, and the package-owned changelog check passes before closure. Its managed contribution inventory now includes changelog contracts, so the real version/contribution change is retained as generated metadata. No changelog generator code is added or patched in pm-cli; upstream pm-changelog currently has no open issues or PRs."
