body: "Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1571\n\nIntake only: reporter reproduction below has not yet been independently run against main. The item remains open and unclaimed. This report arrived after PR #1570 merged and is distinct from its flag-default discovery fixes.\n\n## Summary\n\nFields registered by an extension through `registerItemFields` are persisted and returned by full reads, but `get`/`list`/`search` field projection refuses them as unknown. An agent that needs one custom value must make a refused call and then a full read, which pulls the whole item into context.\n\n## Reproduction (pm 2026.10.24, plain directory, no git)\n\n```ts\nimport { PmClient } from '@unbrained/pm-cli';\nimport { mkdir, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\nconst cwd = resolve('custom-repro'); const ext = resolve('custom-repro/ext');\nawait mkdir(ext, { recursive: true });\nawait writeFile(ext + '/package.json', JSON.stringify({ name: 'probe-field', version: '0.1.0', type: 'module' }));\nawait writeFile(ext + '/manifest.json', JSON.stringify({ name: 'probe-field', version: '0.1.0', manifest_version: 2, entry: './index.ts', capabilities: ['schema'] }));\nawait writeFile(ext + '/index.ts', `import {defineExtension} from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/authoring';\nexport default defineExtension({activate(api){api.registerItemFields([{name:'probe_score',type:'number',optional:true}]);}});`);\nconst c = new PmClient({ cwd, pmRoot: cwd + '/.agents/pm', author: 'probe' });\nawait c.init(undefined, { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip' });\nawait c.packageInstall(ext);\nconst id = (await c.create({ type: 'Task', title: 'Probe', field: ['probe_score=3'] })).item.id;\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(await c.get(id, { full: true })).includes('\"probe_score\":3')); // true\nawait c.get(id, { fields: 'id,probe_score' }); // throws\n```\n\n## Observed\n\n- The full read contains `probe_score: 3`.\n- `get(id, { fields: 'id,probe_score' })` throws `PmCliError: Unknown get --fields value(s): probe_score`. The CLI form (`pm get <id> --fields id,probe_score`) and projected `list`/`search` refuse the same way (`unknown_field_projection`, exit 2).\n- The suggested recovery drops the requested field. The retried query is valid but cannot answer the question.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe set of projectable fields includes the active runtime custom-field registry, the same way in the SDK and the CLI, and keeps the key, type and value. If projecting custom fields is deliberately unsupported, the refusal should say so and point to a read that actually returns the value.\n\n## Cost\n\nRecovering one numeric field takes two calls and about 6.5 KB of output (a 5.1 KB refusal plus a 1.4 KB full read), about 1,600 tokens. Projected `list` and `search` refusals are 4.7 KB and 6.2 KB. Any package that stores typed data in custom fields (pm-rl scores, pm-jev decisions, pm-evidence fingerprints) forces full reads into agent context.\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nSearched `registerItemFields`, `custom field projection`, `unknown_field_projection` and `fields custom registered` (all states). #97 and #839 (setting and typing custom fields) are fixed. #156, #1364 and #1386 cover context depth and projection recovery for built-in fields, not runtime-registered ones."
